ready1_open_rewrite.raw_answer_text:
\textbf{Solution:} Given $EF \parallel AB$, $EF=16$. Draw $OC \perp AB$ at point $C$, intersecting $EF$ at point $G$. Connect $OE$.

$\therefore OC \perp EF$,

$\therefore \angle OGE=\angle OCB=90^\circ$, $BC=\frac{1}{2}AB=6$, $EG=\frac{1}{2}EF=8$,

In $\triangle OCB$, $OC=\sqrt{OB^{2}-CB^{2}}=\sqrt{10^{2}-6^{2}}=8$;

In $\triangle EOG$, $OG=\sqrt{OE^{2}-EG^{2}}=\sqrt{10^{2}-8^{2}}=6$

When $EF$ and $AB$ are on the same side of the center $O$, $CG=OC-OG=8-6=2$;

When $EF$ and $AB$ are on opposite sides of the center $O$, $CG=OC+OG=8+6=14$;

$\therefore$ When the width of the water surface $AB$ changes to 16, the height by which the water surface $AB$ rises is $\boxed{2}$ or 14.

